er-yield tumor sampling approaches</li>\n          <li>Selection of alternative clinical settings can be envisioned</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"footer\">\n      <span>Background</span>\n      <span>Study Design</span>\n      <span>Result</span>\n      <span class=\"active\">Conclusion</span>\n    </footer>\n    <span class=\"page-number\">39</span>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"slide slide-two\">\n    <nav class=\"top-nav\">\n      <span>Novelty &amp; Significance</span>\n      <span class=\"active\">Limitations of the Study</span>\n      <span>Future Work</span>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main class=\"content\">\n      <h1>Limitations</h1>\n\n      <div class=\"section\">\n        <div class=\"section-title\">\n          <span class=\"marker\">c.</span>It is unclear whether pre-vaccine nivolumab contributed to vaccine-<br>\n          induced T cell responses:\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bullet\">\n          Major pathologic responses were noted post-vaccination melanoma<br>\n          patients who did not initially respond to nivolumab.\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"refine\">\n          <span class=\"arrow\">→</span>Refining the sequence of different agents in combination<br>\n          immunotherapy for best clinical outcomes needs further study.\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"check-item\">\n          Alternative immunologic agents, such as anti-CTLA-4, that can preferentially<br>\n          expand naive CD8+ T cells to increase the T cell pool for vaccine priming, might be<br>\n          better a choice for pre-vaccine immunotherapy.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"footer\">\n      <span>Background</span>\n      <span>Study Design</span>\n      <span>Result</span>\n      <span class=\"active\">Conclusion</span>\n    </footer>\n    <span class=\"page-number\">40</span>\n  </section>\n</body>\n</html>"
